01:40:44,490 --> 01:40:45,650
You just had to hit me!

1626
01:40:46,970 --> 01:40:47,770
Bastard!

1627
01:40:48,190 --> 01:40:50,090
You can burn alive, yes.

1628
01:40:50,890 --> 01:40:51,950
Don't care.

1629
01:40:57,410 --> 01:40:58,210
Oh!

1630
01:41:00,310 --> 01:41:01,310
Wait a minute.

1631
01:41:03,890 --> 01:41:05,450
Is that...?

1632
01:41:05,450 --> 01:41:06,110
No.

1633
01:41:06,530 --> 01:41:06,910
Okay.

1634
01:41:11,280 --> 01:41:12,280
I... I need to go up.

1635
01:41:12,360 --> 01:41:12,740
I need to go up.

1636
01:41:13,560 --> 01:41:14,100
You know what?

1637
01:41:14,380 --> 01:41:17,380
Being high up is actually a good idea because I was flying around, remember?

1638
01:41:18,120 --> 01:41:20,780
So I was on top of mountains quite a lot.

1639
01:41:21,860 --> 01:41:22,960
And that's how I navigated.

1640
01:41:23,060 --> 01:41:25,100
So when I go up here, hopefully I'll see something I recognize.

1641
01:41:31,140 --> 01:41:33,520
Okay, that thing, we recognize that.

1642
01:41:36,200 --> 01:41:37,000
That way, then.

1643
01:41:37,840 --> 01:41:38,700
This, I remember.

1644
01:41:38,840 --> 01:41:39,960
All of this is totally fine.

1645
01:41:40,600 --> 01:41:41,960
I was here, 100%.

1646
01:41:41,960 --> 01:41:42,980
No problem.

1647
01:41:45,360 --> 01:41:47,960
But... when we hit the open water, that's the issue.

1648
01:41:52,120 --> 01:41:55,300
I do remember having that floating thing on my right.

1649
01:41:55,700 --> 01:41:58,380
So me being here instead of all the way over there is actually good.

1650
01:42:05,670 --> 01:42:07,710
Yeah, yeah, this is looking better.

1651
01:42:14,050 --> 01:42:15,890
Now the question is, did I fly here?

1652
01:42:16,930 --> 01:42:18,730
I can see myself fly across here.

1653
01:42:24,300 --> 01:42:26,420
But let's not jump to conclusions.

1654
01:42:27,820 --> 01:42:28,980
Okay, I'm feeling way better now.

1655
01:42:29,100 --> 01:42:29,440
This is good.

1656
01:42:29,940 --> 01:42:30,900
At least I recognize this.

1657
01:42:33,140 --> 01:42:35,700
Man, being on the open water lost is actually a nightmare.

1658
01:42:36,540 --> 01:42:39,900
Because you have no landmarks, it's really bad.

1659
01:42:42,700 --> 01:42:43,360
Get off.

1660
01:42:43,880 --> 01:42:44,220
Yeah, see?

1661
01:42:44,340 --> 01:42:48,840
Now I have to recharge, but if I do this... I get off here.

1662
01:42:50,940 --> 01:42:52,860
Oh, never mind, there's still a recharge.

1663
01:42:53,260 --> 01:42:53,640
Huh.

1664
01:42:54,800 --> 01:42:55,620
Maybe I was wrong.

1665
01:42:59,080 --> 01:43:01,080
I thought I discovered something new about the game there.

1666
01:43:02,800 --> 01:43:03,660
Guess I didn't.

1667
01:43:07,940 --> 01:43:09,140
Now what did I do here?

1668
01:43:10,940 --> 01:43:12,460
Let's assume I kept going straight.

1669
01:43:16,170 --> 01:43:21,290
I kind of remember this biome on my right, as I'm seeing it now.

1670
01:43:22,770 --> 01:43:25,850
But I can't really trust my own memory all that much.

1671
01:43:27,150 --> 01:43:29,570
Eyewitness testimony is the worst testimony ever.

1672
01:43:30,470 --> 01:43:34,170
Memory is unreliable AF, as you've seen today.

1673
01:43:38,170 --> 01:43:40,310
So that could just be from one of my dreams, you know?

1674
01:43:45,690 --> 01:43:46,210
Go here.

1675
01:43:48,550 --> 01:43:49,610
Okay, what do we have over here?

1676
01:43:50,690 --> 01:43:52,110
What the fuck is going on up there?

1677
01:43:52,150 --> 01:43:52,770
Is that a portal?

1678
01:43:55,470 --> 01:43:56,130
Yes, it is.

1679
01:43:57,670 --> 01:44:01,010
Guys, I want to check out that chest and then get a good look from up there.

1680
01:44:03,810 --> 01:44:07,610
But... No, actually, no, no, no, we're not doing that.

1681
01:44:08,330 --> 01:44:09,810
I want to stick to this line here.

1682
01:44:10,010 --> 01:44:10,330
Let me see.

1683
01:44:12,910 --> 01:44:13,230
Okay.

1684
01:44:14,740 --> 01:44:17,660
I think I've been here where... I boated across here.

1685
01:44:20,780 --> 01:44:23,120
That is a funny-looking up there, isn't it?

1686
01:44:23,220 --> 01:44:23,920
Funny-looking portal.

1687
01:44:27,780 --> 01:44:28,780
Very, very funny.

1688
01:44:34,280 --> 01:44:37,780
This channel gives me... good memories.

1689
01:44:39,260 --> 01:44:41,480
Oh, but if I was here, I would have grabbed this, wouldn't I?

1690
01:44:45,040 --> 01:44:45,880
Or maybe not.

1691
01:44:54,160 --> 01:44:55,380
Did I go here?

1692
01:44:56,460 --> 01:45:00,420
Man, where the... What kind of route did I take on the open sea just now?

1693
01:45:04,260 --> 01:45:05,000
Hella weird.

1694
01:45:12,230 --> 01:45:13,190
Where am I going?

1695
01:45:15,230 --> 01:45:17,590
I need to see very big mountains, by the way.

1696
01:45:17,930 --> 01:45:20,270
That's when I know I'm in the right spot.

1697
01:45:23,450 --> 01:45:25,190
Do I remember... I don't remember this.

1698
01:45:26,110 --> 01:45:26,950
I don't.

1699
01:45:27,910 --> 01:45:28,710
Not at all.

1700
01:45:30,790 --> 01:45:31,670
No memory.

1701
01:45:33,270 --> 01:45:35,170
That is not a common sight.

1702
01:45:45,960 --> 01:45:47,000
Show me the water now.

1703
01:45:47,160 --> 01:45:47,420
I'm ready.

1704
01:45:49,760 --> 01:45:50,960
I'm ready for the open sea.

1705
01:45:52,660 --> 01:45:54,900
My mouth is open, my tummy is empty.

1706
01:45:55,920 --> 01:45:58,980
Flow into me and fill up my tummy with sea water.

1707
01:46:00,340 --> 01:46:01,460
Fill up that belly.

1708
01:46:04,720 --> 01:46:05,520
There we go.

1709
01:46:06,580 --> 01:46:07,960
Okay, so now we hit the water.

1710
01:46:12,220 --> 01:46:13,220
What did I do?

1711
01:46:14,620 --> 01:46:16,700
What any sane man would do, of course.

1712
01:46:17,380 --> 01:46:20,020
I plopped down my... No!

1713
01:46:20,840 --> 01:46:22,360
It's the cliffs of Dover!

1714
01:46:23,560 --> 01:46:24,120
Fuck!

1715
01:46:25,700 --> 01:46:26,700
But you know what?

1716
01:46:29,060 --> 01:46:35,820
Maybe being so close to it... is what I did, and that's why I missed the island over there.

1717
01:46:37,630 --> 01:46:38,050
Yo!

1718
01:46:38,650 --> 01:46:39,450
Oh, wait, wait, wait, wait.

1719
01:46:39,610 --> 01:46:40,730
We actually have a mountain over there.

1720
01:46:42,530 --> 01:46:45,850
Did I go all the way over... Hold on a second now.

1721
01:46:46,730 --> 01:46:47,570
I'm gonna... Okay.

1722
01:46:51,230 --> 01:46:51,870
Let me see.

1723
01:46:51,970 --> 01:46:52,810
When is it aligned?

1724
01:46:53,450 --> 01:46:55,630
Actually, we're pretty much aligned now with home.

1725
01:46:57,670 --> 01:46:58,630
Oh my god!

1726
01:47:00,790 --> 01:47:04,930
Guys, I actually stumbled around in my chair just now.

1727
01:47:08,330 --> 01:47:13,990
I somehow slipped, like my feet slipped on the floor and I fell backwards in my chair.

1728
01:47:15,470 --> 01:47:18,450
Oh my god, that scared me so much.

1729
01:47:19,050 --> 01:47:23,330
It was just a freaking bubble generator underwater.

1730
01:47:24,350 --> 01:47:24,890
Oh my.

1731
01:47:25,930 --> 01:47:30,110
God damn it, my mouse is... Yeah, okay, we're back.

1732
01:47:30,850 --> 01:47:31,870
Sorry about that.

1733
01:47:36,480 --> 01:47:38,860
Why did I have such a reaction to that?

1734
01:47:39,540 --> 01:47:40,360
That's insane.

1735
01:47:44,260 --> 01:47:45,100
See, here's the thing.

1736
01:47:45,200 --> 01:47:46,480
If I was here, I would have taken this.

1737
01:47:48,760 --> 01:47:49,160
Right?

1738
01:47:51,940 --> 01:47:52,820
Maybe I wasn't here?

1739
01:47:55,220 --> 01:47:56,380
What is that over there?

1740
01:48:02,910 --> 01:48:05,070
Okay, this is where things get a little dicey.

1741
01:48:08,650 --> 01:48:09,830
Ah, fuck.

1742
01:48:10,050 --> 01:48:10,190
Okay.

1743
01:48:10,710 --> 01:48:11,170
You know what?

1744
01:48:11,330 --> 01:48:12,130
Keep going straight.

1745
01:48:12,370 --> 01:48:15,870
If we hit the same shit we saw last time, I'm gonna go right this time instead of left.

1746
01:48:17,010 --> 01:48:17,650
That's the deal.

1747
01:48:20,330 --> 01:48:21,930
This doesn't bring up any memories, though.

1748
01:48:22,030 --> 01:48:22,990
That's really bad.

1749
01:48:24,910 --> 01:48:25,450
Uh-oh.

1750
01:48:28,460 --> 01:48:30,420
And what is that over there?

1751
01:48:30,500 --> 01:48:31,260
Are you seeing this?

1752
01:48:33,220 --> 01:48:34,460
Looks like a tower.

1753
01:48:36,540 --> 01:48:38,200
What the heck is that?

1754
01:48:41,680 --> 01:48:43,000
Looks like windows.

1755
01:48:45,560 --> 01:48:46,160
XP.

1756
01:48:48,120 --> 01:48:49,600
What the fuck?

1757
01:48:55,120 --> 01:48:56,520
Oh, it's just one of those things.

1758
01:48:56,960 --> 01:48:58,900
It looked like a watchtower of some sort.

1759
01:49:01,920 --> 01:49:03,180
I'm gonna go steal your shit.

1760
01:49:05,260 --> 01:49:05,660
Sorry.

1761
01:49:06,360 --> 01:49:09,060
Just gonna... Oh god, I can't, I can't, I can't!

1762
01:49:11,000 --> 01:49:12,660
They're dying in the lava thing!

1763
01:49:14,200 --> 01:49:17,240
You know what, fuck it, I don't want to destroy that piece of rock.

1764
01:49:17,440 --> 01:49:18,200
I'm just gonna keep going.

1765
01:49:19,660 --> 01:49:20,760
Am I though, am I?

1766
01:49:22,000 --> 01:49:22,920
Yeah, I am.

1767
01:49:24,200 --> 01:49:25,620
I will resist the temptation.

1768
01:49:26,680 --> 01:49:29,880
Guys, this doesn't ring any bells.

1769
01:49:31,430 --> 01:49:34,250
What the fuck did I do once I hit open sea?

1770
01:49:36,050 --> 01:49:37,610
There's no way this is real.

1771
01:49:39,230 --> 01:49:41,390
Unless I didn't hit open sea at first.

1772
01:49:41,570 --> 01:49:42,550
Maybe I went across here.

1773
01:49:44,010 --> 01:49:46,750
And then I kept going and there was another open sea.

1774
01:49:47,810 --> 01:49:49,250
Is that what I did?

1775
01:49:50,510 --> 01:49:54,590
I'm open to... to new thoughts now.

1776
01:49:55,560 --> 01:49:59,960
Because I was locked in my mind thinking this had to be that open sea, you know?

1777
01:50:00,160 --> 01:50:01,000
Maybe I'm wrong.

1778
01:50:02,640 --> 01:50:04,160
Maybe I'm completely wrong about that.

1779
01:50:05,360 --> 01:50:06,520
Trust in the instruments.

1780
01:50:06,660 --> 01:50:07,100
IFR.

1781
01:50:17,830 --> 01:50:18,390
Okay.

1782
01:50:18,930 --> 01:50:21,010
Yeah, I actually kind of remember this.

1783
01:50:23,570 --> 01:50:25,370
But I'm not gonna trust that memory.

1784
01:50:26,550 --> 01:50:27,330
Disregard that.

1785
01:50:34,730 --> 01:50:35,450
Get off.

1786
01:50:41,020 --> 01:50:42,660
Okay, up here, here, here.

1787
01:50:45,040 --> 01:50:46,560
We have six fish left.

1788
01:50:46,700 --> 01:50:47,560
It's not actually that much.

1789
01:50:47,660 --> 01:50:48,400
That's all my food.

1790
01:50:49,140 --> 01:50:50,100
I should not run.

1791
01:50:57,380 --> 01:50:58,640
Do I remember this?

1792
01:51:00,900 --> 01:51:01,660
Don't think so.

1793
01:51:03,040 --> 01:51:05,420
And by the way, where the hell...

1794
01:51:08,380 --> 01:51:11,120
Is that... Is that overhang?

1795
01:51:12,200 --> 01:51:13,660
I never got to that overhang.

1796
01:51:16,700 --> 01:51:17,580
Maybe it doesn't matter.

1797
01:51:18,000 --> 01:51:18,960
I think I passed it.

1798
01:51:24,840 --> 01:51:28,360
It is also possible that the open sea that I remember wasn't as big as I thought.

1799
01:51:36,880 --> 01:51:37,280
Sleep.

1800
01:51:37,280 --> 01:51:38,820
Wait, is this guy approaching from the right?

1801
01:51:42,420 --> 01:51:42,820
Okay.

1802
01:51:43,620 --> 01:51:44,540
They are creeping, right?

1803
01:51:45,860 --> 01:51:47,240
So... Gotta be careful.

1804
01:51:58,430 --> 01:52:00,230
What am I seeing?

1805
01:52:02,070 --> 01:52:04,370
This is going to be really exciting now.

1806
01:52:04,570 --> 01:52:06,270
What will I see when I get up high?

1807
01:52:08,950 --> 01:52:10,290
Something memorable, please.

1808
01:52:13,710 --> 01:52:16,450
These birch trees, not memorable at all!

1809
01:52:20,030 --> 01:52:21,090
This is bad.

1810
01:52:25,720 --> 01:52:27,120
No memory of the birch.

1811
01:52:32,980 --> 01:52:34,640
I do have memory of snow, though.

1812
01:52:34,760 --> 01:52:35,400
Maybe I went up there.

1813
01:52:37,880 --> 01:52:39,760
And that way I missed these.

1814
01:52:44,600 --> 01:52:48,280
Village on the mountain is kind of memorable.

1815
01:52:50,220 --> 01:52:51,440
Hold up now.

1816
01:52:54,570 --> 01:52:55,650
This could be it.

1817
01:52:59,320 --> 01:53:02,060
I remember them having one pink tree.

1818
01:53:03,620 --> 01:53:04,620
I remember the ship!

1819
01:53:06,300 --> 01:53:08,500
Oh, guys, we're on the right track!

1820
01:53:10,160 --> 01:53:15,080
When I have so many memories coming back, flooding in like this, you know it's the right path.

1821
01:53:16,160 --> 01:53:17,200
You just know it is.

1822
01:53:17,980 --> 01:53:19,320
This is totally it.

1823
01:53:19,900 --> 01:53:23,900
I went up there, talked to the people, and this is the open sea.

1824
01:53:27,810 --> 01:53:28,990
Oh, yeah.

1825
01:53:29,590 --> 01:53:30,110
Yes!

1826
01:53:31,250 --> 01:53:32,110
This portal.

1827
01:53:32,750 --> 01:53:34,090
Look, the gold is gone!

1828
01:53:35,330 --> 01:53:36,470
I took that.

1829
01:53:36,830 --> 01:53:38,390
And remember this?

1830
01:53:38,630 --> 01:53:39,490
I remember that.

1831
01:53:39,650 --> 01:53:39,850
Everything.

1832
01:53:40,050 --> 01:53:40,790
Oh, we're back.

1833
01:53:41,010 --> 01:53:41,650
We're back!

1834
01:53:42,170 --> 01:53:42,730
Yes!

1835
01:53:43,030 --> 01:53:43,450
Ha-ha!

1836
01:53:44,170 --> 01:53:46,530
Let's not celebrate too early.

1837
01:53:46,670 --> 01:53:46,930
Oh!

1838
01:53:47,730 --> 01:53:48,530
Look at that!

1839
01:53:48,630 --> 01:53:50,010
It's the tower that I destroyed!

1840
01:53:50,190 --> 01:53:51,470
I completely forgot about that!

1841
01:53:51,870 --> 01:53:52,950
It's over there!

1842
01:53:54,010 --> 01:53:55,090
I did that.

1843
01:53:56,430 --> 01:53:57,670
Let's follow in those footsteps.

1844
01:54:00,750 --> 01:54:01,950
Oh, yes, baby.

1845
01:54:03,830 --> 01:54:08,090
So if I was over there, I must have gone to the ocean from there, so let me go over there.

1846
01:54:09,010 --> 01:54:09,510
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1847
01:54:11,450 --> 01:54:12,630
Oh, this is great.

1848
01:54:13,870 --> 01:54:14,590
Yes, sir.

1849
01:54:14,710 --> 01:54:14,870
See?

1850
01:54:15,490 --> 01:54:17,070
That's why you can't trust memories.

1851
01:54:18,410 --> 01:54:22,890
In my mind, I was so convinced that this part that we're in right now...

1852
01:54:23,210 --> 01:54:26,250
Was the part I was in earlier, when I first encountered water.

1853
01:54:27,950 --> 01:54:34,070
So, and because I thought that way, I completely disregarded the idea that it was a second ocean.

1854
01:54:35,670 --> 01:54:36,930
That's called tunnel vision.

1855
01:54:37,830 --> 01:54:41,490
When you disregard everything else but one single line of thought, right?

1856
01:54:41,870 --> 01:54:43,990
Because you're so sure about it, it's so dangerous.

1857
01:54:45,130 --> 01:54:46,990
I definitely checked that out as well.

1858
01:54:51,070 --> 01:54:51,590
Hmm...

1859
01:54:54,110 --> 01:54:55,890
So I must have gone to the ocean from here.

1860
01:54:58,550 --> 01:55:02,510
So now we should see a jungle island very soon.

1861
01:55:07,610 --> 01:55:10,630
Also, my 15 minutes item prediction was a little bit off, wasn't it?

1862
01:55:13,110 --> 01:55:13,870
That was a bummer.

1863
01:55:13,970 --> 01:55:20,630
That's one of my few mistakes that I've made when it comes to predicting things.

1864
01:55:21,870 --> 01:55:22,790
I was off on that.

1865
01:55:23,110 --> 01:55:23,690
That's on me.

1866
01:55:28,280 --> 01:55:29,400
Okay, now we gotta be careful.

1867
01:55:29,620 --> 01:55:30,700
I go straight line now.

1868
01:55:31,540 --> 01:55:34,540
If we don't see anything, I may have to come back.

1869
01:55:35,520 --> 01:55:37,080
That over there looks super interesting.

1870
01:55:39,600 --> 01:55:40,460
No, it doesn't.

1871
01:55:40,620 --> 01:55:40,900
Never mind.

1872
01:55:44,040 --> 01:55:44,860
You know what's fun?

1873
01:55:45,500 --> 01:55:46,280
Look over there.

1874
01:55:46,740 --> 01:55:48,200
You cannot see what's going on.

1875
01:55:48,300 --> 01:55:53,580
But if I move the screen... Can you notice how it's much more zoomed now?

1876
01:55:55,760 --> 01:55:56,660
That's a little trick.

1877
01:56:02,050 --> 01:56:02,930
Oh, wait a minute.

1878
01:56:03,010 --> 01:56:04,730
Is this also where I went diving?

1879
01:56:07,410 --> 01:56:08,950
I completely forgot about that too.

1880
01:56:09,030 --> 01:56:09,830
I did that as well.

1881
01:56:11,170 --> 01:56:12,830
I went diving somewhere here.

1882
01:56:14,270 --> 01:56:16,530
With the potion of water breathing.

1883
01:56:19,610 --> 01:56:20,050
Where?

1884
01:56:20,230 --> 01:56:20,770
I don't know.

1885
01:56:20,930 --> 01:56:21,790
But somewhere here, you know?

1886
01:56:25,110 --> 01:56:26,190
There it is!

1887
01:56:26,970 --> 01:56:29,030
Oh, what a beautiful sight!

1888
01:56:29,290 --> 01:56:31,450
That is exactly like my dreams.

1889
01:56:33,110 --> 01:56:35,290
Look at that.

1890
01:56:38,650 --> 01:56:39,590
